  "answer":"After a significant drift is detected, the production checklist requires that a challenger model be trained and evaluated, and that a control batch be evaluated before any alerts are trusted. Promotion of a new model is only allowed when the challenger meets the release‑policy thresholds on a frozen holdout set: its F1 score must improve by at least 0.005 and its ROC‑AUC must not drop by more than 0.01. A drift alert by itself does not authorize promotion; the release approver (the project owner) must also approve the change.",
